    "fileId": 33471,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Differential diagnoses of B-cell and T-cell lymphomas/leukaemias</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Werner Kempf",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histopathological features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Immunohistochemical and molecular features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Primary cutaneous follicle centre cell lymphoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Large neoplastic follicle or diffuse infiltrates of tumour cells with predominantly centrocytoid differentiation, lack of polarization, and absence of tingible body macrophages in the neoplastic follicles</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Tumour cells: BCL6+, BCL2&minus;, CD10+/&minus;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Irregular networks of CD21+ or CD35+ FDCs</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Secondary cutaneous involvement by nodal follicular lymphoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histology identical to that of primary cutaneous follicle centre cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Tumour cells: coexpression of BCL6 and BCL2</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">t(14;18) translocation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Secondary cutaneous MZL&nbsp;/ EMZL of MALT</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Often large sheets of B&nbsp;cells, predominance of monocytoid B&nbsp;cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">IgM+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cutaneous involvement in B-cell chronic lymphocytic leukaemia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Monotonous infiltrates of small B&nbsp;cells, often in close vicinity to epithelial skin neoplasias</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Detection of circulating tumour cells in the peripheral blood</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Tumour cells: coexpression of B-cell markers, CD5, CD23, and CD43</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Secondary cutaneous mantle cell lymphoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Dermal and/or subcutaneous infiltrates of atypical lymphocytes of variable size</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-ansi-language: FR;\">Tumour cells: cyclin&nbsp;D1+ or SOX11</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-ansi-language: FR;\">t(11;14)(q13;q32) translocation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Secondary cutaneous lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Monotonous infiltrates of small lymphoplasmacytoid cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Frequent Dutcher bodies</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">MYD88</span></em><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> p.L256P mutation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-titre IgM paraproteinaemia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Marrow involvement</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Primary cutaneous CD4+ small&nbsp;/ medium-sized lymphoproliferative disorder</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Dermal nodular infiltrate of small CD4+ lymphocytes with admixture of small to medium-sized PD1+ T&nbsp;cells, aggregates of B&nbsp;cells, rarely germinal centre formation, polytypic plasma cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">T&nbsp;cells: CD4+, partially PD1+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">B&nbsp;cells: CD20+, PAX5+, BCL2+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clonal rearrangement of TR&nbsp;genes</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">EMZL, extranodal marginal zone lymphoma; FDC, follicular dendritic cell; MALT, mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue; MZL, marginal zone lymphoma.</span></p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 64201,
    "bookid": 64,
    "chapterId": 185,
    "fileId": 39122,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Primary cutaneous marginal zone lymphoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "No epidermal involvement, subepidermal grenz zone. Nodular dermal lymphocytic infiltrate with periadnexal and perivascular accentuation. Small lymphocytes and lymphoplasmacytoid cells. Plasma cells are found in the edge of the infiltrates and next to the epidermis.",
    "source": "Rajendra Singh",
